meta {
  name: Start from an empty cart
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/cart
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.isEmpty: eq true
}

docs {
  Housekeeping, not a test of clearing -- that is the last request in the folder.

  Measured: the CLI's cookie jar is per-run and in memory, so `bru run` always starts as a
  brand-new visitor with an empty cart and this request is a no-op there. The Bruno GUI is
  the opposite -- its jar persists, so without this the second run in a desktop session
  would start with the leftovers of the first and every quantity below would be wrong.
  One request buys a folder that means the same thing in both.
}
